ame a normal part of our relationship  and where it started to becoming not  normal is when he started lying about it  and starting to hide it because it was  excessive but I had gotten in the habit  of going yep let's go get a drink or two  drink or two became four five six seven  eight and watching that  was heartbreaking because I knew  I knew it was tanking him  our wedding night was not like the  typical wedding night that a girl dreams  of but we went out and we met up with  some of the people that we worked with  and some friends in Savannah and  downtown and the drinks just kept  flowing and when we got up to her room  he was in full anger mode he was lashing  out he was throwing things across the  room screaming every kind of name even  had knocked me over a few times and I I  think I maybe got an hour of sleep that  night and to the point where he woke up  and I was sitting there looking at him  and I just said I don't know if I can do  this I love you and I want to do this  but I don't know if I can and I left on  that Sunday morning  knowing I wouldn't leave him but knowing  that if something didn't change  immediately like Monday and I don't mean  like his pts would be gone on Monday but  that he would take active steps on  Monday that I couldn't stay with someone  who could hurt me  [Music]  didn't know it's hurting me as well  [Music]  Monday morning I got a call from Tom and  he said he had gotten an appointment  like had begged this therapist to fit  him in and I think literally that day  like that afternoon he went and saw  someone  the first thing I saw in him was A  Renewed hope in himself that he trusted  himself in a way that I hadn't really  seen before he was making better choices  and to this day I think he's done nine  or ten different types of therapies and  treatments which is necessary with  complex pts there's not one thing that  can take care of all of it I've been so  proud of him for tackling each and every  treatment just like he's 