hy I would hear about  some combat trauma that it's not what  was coming forward mostly what was  coming forward mostly was I don't know  how to be a good father I don't know how  to be a good husband I do this job  really really well and I'm trained for  it I have a manual for it I know what to  do and I've got the guy to my left and  right that's going to help me if I don't  know what to do but when I go home I'm  all alone and I don't have a manual and  I don't know what to do  it was in 2016 on the last exercise that  I had done the last rmt and I pulled Tom  aside and I said I want to start a  non-profit because I frankly didn't want  to send guys off to war anymore I didn't  want to watch it I didn't want to  participate in it was breaking my heart  over and over and over again not just  the loss that I was seeing but truly  seeing people come back different people  that I had seen rotation after rotation  they were coming back different  different and different 28 years old  looking 48 years old just in a matter of  three years and two divorces had gone by  and I thought I can't do this anymore I  can't help our men and women go off to  fight I need to help them come home  somebody has to help them come home they  deserve it and so do their families  [Music]  here  [Music]  [Music]  what's the process Monday and they've  been waiting how long  uh secure Foundation serves Special  Operation Warriors and their families  and healing from complex pts and  secondary PTS  nobody should have to battle this alone  it's no different than breaking your arm  if you break your arm you're going to  see a doctor you're going to get  treatment for it and you're going to get  better and it's the exact same thing  with pts when you have an injury due to  trauma treat it immediately and you'll  get better from it the longer you wait  or shoving under the rug doesn't work it  gets worse with time not better  I'll secure Foundation was founded from  truly a hope that we can join